  "details": "Since the new patch went live any time someone joins a world, or if I join a world, my client will hang due to the game trying to go out to retrieve something for their avatar and waiting instead of doing the job asynchronously.  This results in high-population worlds (eg; The Great Pug) being unvisitable, because VRChat will just sit and wait for 20-odd player's worth of whatever it's sending requests for, and times out the server times out the client in the meantime.  As best I can tell looking at the output log, the culprit lies in the Amplitude API;\n\n2020.04.13 02:53:00 Error      -  AmplitudeAPI: upload failed with exception - Connection refused\n  at System.Net.Sockets.SocketAsyncResult.CheckIfThrowDelayedException () [0x00000] in <00000000000000000000000000000000>:0 \n  at VRC.Core.BestHTTP.PlatformSupport.TcpClient.General.TcpClient.Connect (System.Net.IPEndPoint remoteEP) [0x00000] in <00000000000000000000000000000000>:0 \n  at VRC.Core.BestHTTP.PlatformSupport.TcpClient.General.TcpClient.Connect (System.Net.IPAddress[] ipAddresses, System.Int32 port) [0x00000] in <00000000000000000000000000000000>:0 \n  at VRC.Core.BestHTTP.HTTPConnection.Connect () [0x00000] in <00000000000000000000000000000000>:0 \n  at VRC.Core.BestHTTP.HTTPConnection.ThreadFunc (System.Object param) [0x00000] in <00000000000000000000000000000000>:0 \n  at System.Threading.ExecutionContext.RunInternal (System.Threading.ExecutionContext executionContext, System.Threading.ContextCallback callback, System.Object state, System.Boolean preserveSyncCtx) [0x00000] in <00000000000000000000000000000000>:0 \n  at System.Threading.ExecutionContext.Run (System.Threading.ExecutionContext executionContext, System.Threading.ContextCallback callback, System.Object state) [0x00000] in <00000000000000000000000000000000>:0 \n\n2020.04.13 02:53:00 Error      -  AmplitudeAPI: UpdateServer: unhandleable error code: Exception - discarding this batch of 10 events",
